PieceList renders on every keystroke because two of its props are new on every render of the page. Each keystroke calls setNotes, PracticePage renders again, and it creates a fresh `sort={{ by: "lastPracticed" }}` object and a fresh `onSelect` arrow (t3). memo compares each prop with Object.is, so both count as changed, and the useMemo inside PieceList (t4) re-sorts the list as well.

The fix I'd pick is to move the notes box and its state into its own component, so typing only renders that component:

```diff
+function NotesBox() {
+  const [notes, setNotes] = useState("");
+  return <textarea value={notes} onChange={(e) => setNotes(e.target.value)} />;
+}
+
