-  const [notes, setNotes] = useState("");
   const [selectedId, setSelectedId] = useState<string | null>(null);
@@
-      <textarea value={notes} onChange={(e) => setNotes(e.target.value)} />
+      <NotesBox />
```

The other way is to keep the state where it is, move the sort object to a module constant and wrap onSelect in useCallback. That works too, but the next inline prop someone adds breaks it again.

To confirm, turn on "Highlight updates when components render." in the React DevTools settings and type in the box: only the notes box should flash.

